---
/**
 * GetStarted — the standalone "Connect your agent" band.
 *
 * The install paths themselves live in SetupTabs, shared with the hero. This file owns
 * only the framing: the heading, the lede, and the section rhythm.
 *
 * Tabs rather than a card grid, for a structural reason and not a stylistic one. Four
 * paths with 3, 1, 2 and 1 steps and notes of different lengths can only ever be the same
 * height by accident; side by side they read as four ragged boxes. Stacked into one frame
 * they share one alignment, and a reserve holds the frame still while you switch.
 *
 * "Each path gets the full width" was true of that arrangement and is not true now: from
 * 60rem the panel splits `1.45fr / 1fr`, steps left and the supporting note right. What
 * the tabs buy is one frame per path rather than four competing ones, which is the part
 * that survived the split.
 *
 * The rail is underlined rather than pilled to stay distinct from the pill control in
 * AskExamples: two identical widgets doing different jobs read as one widget repeated.
 * That band is currently unmounted, so the clash is latent rather than visible, and the
 * underline stays precisely so remounting it does not reintroduce the collision.
 */
import SetupTabs from './SetupTabs.astro';
---

<section class="gs" id="connect">
  <h2 class="caail-display sr">Connect your agent</h2>
  {/* "Nothing to install" was true while every path was a paste or a CLI command. The
      leading path is now Claude Science, which is an application on a paid plan, so the
      blanket claim had to go: it is CAAIL that needs no hosting or authentication, not
      the client. "The only real difference is how long the setup lasts" went with it for
      the same reason, since eligibility now differs between paths too. */}
  <p class="lede sr sr-d1">
    CAAIL is static JSON on GitHub, so there is nothing to host and nothing to
    authenticate. The paths differ in how long the setup lasts, and in what each one
    asks of you.
  </p>

  <div class="sr sr-d2">
    <SetupTabs idPrefix="gs" />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .gs { margin: var(--caail-section-gap) 0 0; }
  .gs h2 { font-size: var(--caail-fs-h2); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.02em; color: var(--caail-primary); margin: 0 0 var(--caail-space-3); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--caail-fs-base); color: var(--caail-muted); margin: 0 0 var(--caail-space-5); max-width: var(--caail-measure); text-wrap: pretty; }
</style>
